## Course overview

Slovak A: Literature lets students study their first language through its literature - reading Slovak and translated works closely, comparing texts across periods and cultures, and writing with precision and style about how meaning is made.

## What you will study

- **Readers, writers and texts**: how literary form and language create meaning.
- **Time and space**: the cultural and historical contexts that shape works.
- **Intertextuality**: connections and dialogue across texts and traditions.
- A selection of **Slovak and translated world literature** studied in depth.

## Assessment

| Component | SL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (guided literary analysis) | 35% | Guided analysis of an unseen literary passage |
| Paper 2 (comparative essay) | 35% | Comparison of two studied literary works |
| Individual Oral | 30% | Spoken analysis of two literary works |
